  (:id "platforms"
   :title "Platforms"
   :text "Where RocketNet builds and passes. Every push runs the unit and functional suites on Linux, macOS and Windows; the nightly jobs run on Linux, and their macOS and Windows jobs are not yet enabled."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Per-commit CI, Debug and Release" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: ci.yml ubuntu-24.04 Debug and Release legs, green in runs 39271096164 and 39286548764; those legs run the unit suite, the functional suite on the auto ladder and with the portable rung pinned, and the lifecycle binary" :note "macOS: the macos-15 / Debug leg's Run functional suite (portable rung pinned by env) step is red in run 39286548764, so the cell is n until it is green. Windows runs Release per push (build-and-test-windows), and its Functional suite with IOCP selected step is red in runs 39271096164 and 39286548764; its Debug row is in nightly.yml and disabled")
    (:feature "Shared export list compared" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: the production library boundary step runs tools/check_exports.py in build-and-test and build-and-test-windows; tools/check_exports.py, tools/exports.txt; 095f374 production sources separate from tests, strict endpoint port parsing")
    (:feature "Nightly soak" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: nightly-soak.yml on the Linux runners; nightly-soak.yml; 63a25be macOS; 9ee42a2 Windows" :note "the macOS (63a25be) and Windows (9ee42a2) soak jobs are disabled")
    (:feature "The library is callable from a shared library and a static library, from C and C++" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: tools/check_dll_consumer.py runs in build-and-test (Linux and macOS) and build-and-test-windows on every push; its macOS cases landed with eb50adb and its Windows cases with ae06e12" :note "one row for the macOS and Windows items")))
  (:id "api"
   :title "Public API"
   :text "The C surface in sdk/rocketnet.h and what a consumer needs to use it."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "Connection layer C surface: rocketnet_client_transport_* and rocketnet_server_transport_*" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; ruled #77; sdk/rocketnet.h; packet contexts checked against single-consumption leases: test_lifecycle.cpp check_packet_leases")
    (:feature "Root header pure C: the client and server with their functions, the address type, nothing else" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 5c3027f, dcd941f (6b73068); sdk/rocketnet.h plain C99 with one extern C block; rocketnet_test_public_client_server_queries, rocketnet_test_config_refuses_rocketnet_driver; clean at /W4 and -Wextra 9ead512" :note "ruled: netcode-style, real non-mangled symbols for C and FFI; a C++ inside is an implementation privilege")
    (:feature "Message objects in C: rocketnet_message_client_* and rocketnet_message_server_*" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 2c1aa7b")
    (:feature "Installable CMake package with C and C++ consumers" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; tools/check_package.py, tools/package_consumer")
    (:feature "Vendored sodium, no system libsodium" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 23d4c40; sodium/")
    (:feature "Structured create errors and FFI-safe logging" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; status codes 4e2d6f1 (status_strings_cover_every_code); create_ex 3e82436, b2bc4ea, 33f84d3 (server_transport_create_ex_reports_every_status, client_transport_create_ex_reports_every_status, lifecycle_ex_reports_every_status); preformatted log callback 194ecc5 (log_callback_preformatted_contract)")
    (:feature "Transports are named transports throughout: the rocketnet_*_transport_* calls, ROCKETNET_SERVER_TRANSPORT and ROCKETNET_CLIENT_TRANSPORT, and the documentation" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as 92b6b50a; sdk/rocketnet.h names no driver; test_transport_env_pins_loopback in ./bin/test; Linux: the unit suite is green at 330e951e: ./bin/test exits 0 in a Release build on Linux x86_64, and the ASan and UBSan unit job of CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e passes" :note "macOS: CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e had not yet run the macOS legs when this was recorded, so the cell is n until they are green. Windows: the Windows build is red at 330e951e in CI run 39514217665 (functional/windows_socket_errors.cpp and functional/windows_connreset.cpp call a name the transport rename removed), so the cell is n until the Windows legs are green")
    (:feature "One receive queue per client and one per server, every channel's messages in delivery order, pumped in batches with no release call" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as 3a021484; receive_one_queue_every_type_every_channel, receive_pumped_past_one_batch_in_order, public_not_released_batch_released_by_update in ./bin/test; Linux: the unit suite is green at 330e951e: ./bin/test exits 0 in a Release build on Linux x86_64, and the ASan and UBSan unit job of CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e passes" :note "macOS: CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e had not yet run the macOS legs when this was recorded, so the cell is n until they are green. Windows: the Windows build is red at 330e951e in CI run 39514217665 (functional/windows_socket_errors.cpp and functional/windows_connreset.cpp call a name the transport rename removed), so the cell is n until the Windows legs are green")
    (:feature "Create returns NULL and a status code that names why it refused" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as 7c04293a; rocketnet_client_create and rocketnet_server_create take an enum rocketnet_status_t out-parameter; create_reports_status_success, create_reports_status_invalid_argument, create_reports_status_config_refusals, create_reports_status_out_of_memory and the other create_reports_status_ cases in ./bin/test; Linux: the unit suite is green at 330e951e: ./bin/test exits 0 in a Release build on Linux x86_64, and the ASan and UBSan unit job of CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e passes" :note "macOS: CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e had not yet run the macOS legs when this was recorded, so the cell is n until they are green. Windows: the Windows build is red at 330e951e in CI run 39514217665 (functional/windows_socket_errors.cpp and functional/windows_connreset.cpp call a name the transport rename removed), so the cell is n until the Windows legs are green")
    (:feature "A server serves IPv4, IPv6 or both on one port" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as 1581b134; second_public_address in rocketnet_server_config_t; server_serves_ipv4_and_ipv6_clients_on_one_port, one_family_server_is_unchanged, server_refuses_second_address_of_the_same_family in ./bin/test; Linux: the unit suite is green at 330e951e: ./bin/test exits 0 in a Release build on Linux x86_64, and the ASan and UBSan unit job of CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e passes" :note "macOS: CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e had not yet run the macOS legs when this was recorded, so the cell is n until they are green. Windows: the Windows build is red at 330e951e in CI run 39514217665 (functional/windows_socket_errors.cpp and functional/windows_connreset.cpp call a name the transport rename removed), so the cell is n until the Windows legs are green")
    (:feature "One environment variable per setting, current names only: retired names are not read" :cells (y n n) :evidence "Linux: landed as bd606975 and 5f84b75c, BUILDING.md lists the current names (0158464f); config_env_every_name_read_is_documented, config_env_transport_passes_exercise_all_rows in ./bin/test; Linux: the unit suite is green at 330e951e: ./bin/test exits 0 in a Release build on Linux x86_64, and the ASan and UBSan unit job of CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e passes" :note "macOS: CI run 39514217665 at 330e951e had not yet run the macOS legs when this was recorded, so the cell is n until they are green. Windows: the Windows build is red at 330e951e in CI run 39514217665 (functional/windows_socket_errors.cpp and functional/windows_connreset.cpp call a name the transport rename removed), so the cell is n until the Windows legs are green")
    (:feature "Sized APIs for compatible struct evolution" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; a5941cf; sized_config_accepts_every_known_size, sized_config_refuses_unknown_size; docs/ABI-EVOLUTION.md")
    (:feature "Whole-transport memory estimates and operator budgets (#155)" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; rocketnet_server_required_memory and rocketnet_client_required_memory 1d9f830; the host memory estimate cad7a0c (rocketnet_test_server_host_memory_estimate_bounds_the_plan); operator budgets 227d895 USAGE.md; BUILDING.md Pre-allocation server resource plans" :note "an estimate of what is requested, with its exclusions named (kernel accounting beyond the requests, libbpf and libxdp, guard pages, application memory); not an available-RAM check")
    (:feature "C++ ClientTransport and ServerTransport interfaces" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 925cbd7 cpp_transport_interfaces_map_one_to_one, cpp_transport_fake_implements_the_interface; 8985b00 rocketnet_test_cpp_transports_connect_over_loopback")
    (:feature "Shared library build, checked exports, callable from C and C++" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 73733ad tools/check_header_exports.py; a26fd6c export count derived; a6e3991 tools/check_dll_consumer.py, tools/dll_consumer")
    (:feature "API reference generated by MrDocs" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: a document, built by docs.yml on the Linux runners; baf841d mrdocs.yml, docs/mrdocs, .github/workflows/docs.yml")
    (:feature "API reference comments: platform" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: a document; landed as 2c2fac0")
    (:feature "API reference comments: reliability" :cells (y - -) :evidence "Linux: a document; landed as 90683f2")
