  (:id "standard"
   :title "The standard"
   :text "The normative standard in standard/: standard/TRANSPORT.md (the t sections) and standard/MESSAGES.md (the m sections), each section with its conformance vectors, checked by the unit suite and the conformance job."
   :columns platforms
   :rows
   ((:feature "The normative standard in standard/, a conformance vector per section" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: ci.yml runs ./bin/test and ./bin/functional on the Linux, macOS and Windows legs on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164; 61c0e67 skeleton and tools/conformance/check_rn_standard.py; one change per section, each with its vectors (standard_wire_primitives_vectors 062e2cb through standard_channels_receipts_security_vectors 263a088); standard/RATIONALE.md 3ba4ff2")
    (:feature "Section t6: connect token" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 192db19; its cases run in the unit and functional suites ci.yml runs on all three on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164")
    (:feature "Section t7: key schedule" :cells (y y y) :evidence "Linux, macOS, Windows: landed as 1701719; its cases run in the unit and functional suites ci.yml runs on all three on every push, green on all three in run 39271096164")
